# Ownership is about who must approve, not who may.
#
# The register is a legal document that happens to be JSON. A change to a control, an
# element assertion, an anti-pattern or a band is a change to what the firm asserts about
# a client's statutory position, and it needs a named reviewer who reads statutes - not
# whoever happens to be free. Replace the placeholders below with real handles before
# enabling branch protection; an unresolvable CODEOWNERS entry silently approves nothing.

# Everything, by default
*                               @REPLACE-WITH-LEAD

# The register itself: control text, elements, predicates, bands, lexicon, coverage
/data/registers/                @REPLACE-WITH-LEAD @REPLACE-WITH-SECOND-REVIEWER
/data/profiles/fields.json      @REPLACE-WITH-LEAD @REPLACE-WITH-SECOND-REVIEWER

# Statute snapshots. A diff here is an amendment, and it forces a register review.
/data/sources/                  @REPLACE-WITH-LEAD @REPLACE-WITH-SECOND-REVIEWER

# Architecture decisions. Changing one of these changes how findings are classified.
/docs/adr/                      @REPLACE-WITH-LEAD @REPLACE-WITH-SECOND-REVIEWER

# The client-facing surface. Compliance and legal sign off on page one.
/src/pfia/report/templates/     @REPLACE-WITH-LEAD @REPLACE-WITH-COMPLIANCE
